not  people they're dead  too bad for the walkers but these  circumstances work out splendidly for  those of us here in the real world  hordes of grotesque and gruesome undead  are visually distinctive in a way that  sticks with the viewer long after the tv  has been shut off  we tune into programs like the walking  dead because we want to see the menacing  hordes of the undead and we want to see  them  hideously disfigured in the world of the  walking dead walkers  are terrifying and in a world where a  zombie apocalypse hasn't happened yet  that's exactly what we want walkers  possess several qualities that inhibit  their people-eating abilities while  enhancing their entertainment value  for example in most cases you can hear  them coming from long distances off  due to their apparently compulsive need  to make weird  barfing noises sometimes walkers make  very loud barfing noises and sometimes  they lower the volume of their  barfing noises to a very quiet level but  one truth remains  regardless walkers will make  uncomfortable  guttural noises no matter the situation  they practically never stop making these  noises even though they don't seem to  serve  any purpose for them in fact it gives  away their location  and offers potential human meals plenty  of time to run away  however it does add ominous ambiance and  the walking dead wouldn't quite be  itself without it  walkers can't talk scream or sing in  their hideous version of the afterlife  but they don't need to  because those horrible hissing moans of  theirs haunt  our dreams look if you don't  absolutely love completely uncooked  literally fresh off the bone human meat  then you've got no business being a  walker  it's basically their whole deal walkers  lead boring  bland lives if we're being honest they  indefinitely roam about with no purpose  or direction  until their limited abilities of  detection pick up on one of the  dwindling  number of humans who have not already  been converted into walkers  they only really want one thing and it's  the thing that keeps the danger of the  show going  the flesh of the living the gang of  sympathetic survivors on the walking  dead  often find themselves in life or death  conflicts with groups of malignant  fellow humans  while these plots unfold walkers are  relegated to the background  sometimes in a quite literal sense some  critics don't like this but unless you  just want the walkers to eat people over  and over and over  it's the way it has to be if the walkers  were the only villains on the show it  would just be a constant buffet of human  meat  feasting on human flesh is literally the  whole gig for a walker  this is basically the only rule that  applies to both walkers  and humans if your brain dies you die  no exceptions it doesn't matter whether  you get shot in the face or head  or whether someone pierces your grey  matter with a blade or pointed object  a swift blow of blunt force could also  do the trick as long as it punctures the  protective bone layer and squashes the  wrinkled ball of goo within  in any of these cases that's the end of  the story for you  you can no longer claim the status of  undead you're just well  dead the good news for walkers about  this rule though is that they can  survive virtually  anything up to this point including  having their head flat out removed from  their body  take a walker apart any way you like as  long as they still have a brain working  in their head  they'll just watch you do it which might  be all the more reason to kill the brain  and get it over with  it's simple strategy any walker hoping  to sink their diseased  blunted teeth into a still living  screaming person  needs to find themselves a crew a single  walker might get lucky and stumble  upon an injured human or a very stupid  child every now and again  but most of the time a walker on their  own is basically just a sitting duck for  the next human survivor with a weapon  sticking with a large group doesn't mean  a walker  definitely won't get their brains bashed  in at some point but hanging with a  crowd demonstrably increases their  chances of finding a person  and actually getting a meal out of the  deal people who see a herd of walkers  get scared  run away in a random direction and  sometimes find their way into a dead end  where walkers can descend upon them if  you're a walker doing the lone wolf  thing though you're just as likely to  end up with a machete through your head  so stick with your friends as far as  options for the afterlife go  walker hood is kind of boring you  stumble around looking for fresh meat  and if you find it attempt to shove it  in your face until there's no more meat  apart from that you're just killing time  until someone comes along and  caves in your skull you told me to  handle them easily  this is easy yeah it's easier to  something  being a walker certainly limits your  options but at least it's easy and  low pressure among walkers there's no  hierarchy walkers don't have  walker bosses who tell them what to do  walkers don't get a reward for eating  somebody they just  immediately resume looking for a new  person to eat so whether they eat one  person in a week or 12  it doesn't make any difference it  doesn't matter if you're a successful  walker or  a failure as a walker walkers don't  really compete with each other in fact  if it wasn't for the inevitable violent  demise  total loss of cognitive function and  endless craving for flesh  being a walker would be a pretty relaxed  gig they're comfortable living in the  moment  the awful bloody post-apocalyptic moment  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss  a single one

